<h2 id="an-answer-forms-as-the-network-settles">An answer forms as the network settles</h2>

<p>Picture the cue activating one group of neurons while two other groups represent the possible actions. Connections carry influence in both directions. The cue shapes the network’s interpretation, and the state of the action groups can influence earlier activity while the answer forms. Cadence repeatedly updates this shared state under the current observation. Once the state satisfies the network’s equations within a tolerance, the system can use it to choose an action. This is what the project calls <em>settling</em>. <a href="https://github.com/muellerberndt/cadence/blob/main/docs/settling.md#settling-and-equilibrium">Cadence’s guide to settling</a></p>

